.TH SPOL 8 "2026-11-09" "nni @VERSION@" "nni family manual"
.SH NAME
spol \- Sourced Portage\-Oriented Linker, the SGnniOS package manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spol
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ PACKAGE ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spol
is the friendly face of Portage on SGnniOS: packages are compiled from
source on your machine.
.B emerge
stays available underneath. Package names are Gentoo names,
category/name, for example net\-wireless/iw.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B sync
Fetch the Portage tree and the nni overlay. Do this first.
.TP
.BI install " PACKAGE..."
Build and install.
.TP
.BI reinstall " PACKAGE..."
Rebuild and reinstall (puts deleted files back).
.TP
.BI remove " PACKAGE..."
Uninstall.
.TP
.B autoremove
Remove packages nothing needs.
.TP
.B upgrade
Update the whole system.
.TP
.BI search " TERM"
Search the tree.
.TP
.BI show " PACKAGE"
What would be built, with USE flags.
.TP
.BI use " PACKAGE FLAGS..."
Save USE flags in
.IR /etc/portage/package.use/spol .
Without arguments, show them.
.TP
.BI jobs " N"
Number of parallel compile jobs (MAKEOPTS). Big C++ builds need 1\-2 GB
of memory per job, so lower it if builds run out of memory.
.TP
.BR list ", " files " \fIPACKAGE\fP, " owns " \fIFILE\fP"
Installed packages, their files, and which package owns a file.
.TP
.B clean
Delete downloaded source tarballs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bin
Use a cached binary package when one exists (much faster).
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Do not ask for confirmation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
spol sync
spol search nano
spol install app\-editors/nano
spol jobs 2
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pol (8),
.BR nni (8),
.BR emerge (1)
